EXTRA QUESTIONS
Q: What is the difference between training and testing data?
A: Training data fits the model; testing data evaluates it on unseen examples.

Q: Why use random_state=42?
A: It makes the data split and Random Forest randomness reproducible.

Q: Why is feature scaling useful for SVM?
A: SVM is sensitive to feature scales, so standardization prevents large-range features from dominating.

Q: What is overfitting?
A: When a model learns training data too closely and performs poorly on unseen data.

Q: What is the difference between Random Forest and SVM?
A: Random Forest combines decision trees; SVM learns a separating boundary between classes.

Q: Does feature importance prove causation?
A: No. It measures predictive contribution in the model, not cause and effect.
